    "text": "To determine what percent of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is shaded, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the dimensions of the rectangle:**\n   Let the width of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) be \\(w\\). Since the rectangle is four times as long as it is wide, the length of the rectangle is \\(4w\\).\n\n2. **Identify the coordinates of the points:**\n   - \\(A = (0, 1)\\)\n   - \\(B = (0, 0)\\)\n   - \\(C = (4w, 0)\\)\n   - \\(D = (4w, 1)\\)\n   - \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{BC}\\), so \\(E = (2w, 0)\\)\n\n3. **Determine the area of the rectangle:**\n   The area \\(A_{\\text{rectangle}}\\) of the rectangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{rectangle}} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} = 4w \\times w = 4w^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Identify the shaded regions:**\n   The shaded regions are two right triangles:\n   - Triangle \\(ABE\\)\n   - Triangle \\(DEC\\)\n\n5. **Calculate the area of triangle \\(ABE\\):**\n   - Base \\(AB = w\\)\n   - Height from \\(E\\) to \\(AB\\) is \\(w\\) (since \\(E\\) is at \\(y = 0\\) and \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) are at \\(y = 1\\))\n   The area \\(A_{\\triangle ABE}\\) of triangle \\(ABE\\) is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\triangle ABE} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times w \\times w = \\frac{1}{2}w^2\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the area of triangle \\(DEC\\):**\n   - Base \\(DC = 4w\\)\n   - Height from \\(E\\) to \\(DC\\) is \\(w\\) (since \\(E\\) is at \\(y = 0\\) and \\(D\\) and \\(C\\) are at \\(y = 1\\))\n   The area \\(A_{\\triangle DEC}\\) of triangle \\(DEC\\) is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\triangle DEC} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 4w \\times w = 2w^2\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculate the total shaded area:**\n   The total shaded area is the sum of the areas of the two triangles:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{shaded}} = A_{\\triangle ABE} + A_{\\triangle DEC} = \\frac{1}{2}w^2 + 2w^2 = \\frac{1}{2}w^2 + \\frac{4}{2}w^2 = \\frac{5}{2}w^2\n   \\]\n\n8. **Determine the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded:**\n   The percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage shaded} = \\left( \\frac{A_{\\text{shaded}}}{A_{\\text{rectangle}}} \\right) \\times 100\\%\n   \\]\n   Substituting the areas:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage shaded} = \\left( \\frac{\\frac{5}{2}w^2}{4w^2} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{5}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{4} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{5}{8} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 62.5\\%\n   \\]\n\nThus, the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is \\(\\boxed{62.5}\\).",
